                <pb facs="0345" n="283" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg283"/>

                <head>No. 185.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Welsh to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-08-21"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 21,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Evarts</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Secretary, Washington:</hi></p>
                <p>Salisbury officially informs me the cabinet will recommend Queen to remit
                    remainder of the sentence of Condon and Melody.</p>
                <p>Queen’s action not yet communicated.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <closer><signed>WELSH,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Minister</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
